# Conversational copy

When writing or editing user-facing product text (labels, buttons, cards, empty/error/success, confirms, tooltips, settings descriptions):

1. Apply the `conversational-copy` skill.
2. Keep copy short and human. Prefer the shortest clear line.
3. Do not pad with AI-sounding filler, brochure adjectives, or redundant CTAs the control already implies (e.g. omit "فتح الإعداد" on a whole-card button).
4. Buttons: verb (+ object if needed). Errors: what happened + what to do.
